# Source of truth for the protobuf-6 all-features CI lock: the light tier with [stac], [vizx]
# and [zarr_dbr19], at the versions the env6 runtime family (Serverless env 6 / classic DBR 19)
# preinstalls. (On Databricks those runtimes install the env6 wheel; this lock tests the plain
# wheel's light tier off Databricks with the same versions.)
#
# Regenerate (from python/geobrix/), on any host: the platform is explicit so the result does not
# depend on where it runs (a Linux aarch64 host would otherwise drop the click hold below):
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 \
#       --output-file requirements-light-env6-all-ci.txt requirements-light-env6-all-ci.in
#
# This .in uses a local-package-with-extras reference so uv expands the base dependencies and
# [stac] + [vizx] + [zarr_dbr19] directly from pyproject.toml; the holds below are the env6
# runtimes' versions. ([overture] is opt-in and left out.) Protobuf-5 twin:
# requirements-light-env5-all-ci.in.
#
# Resolved for x86_64 Linux: the `click>=8.2,<8.3` hold applies (it is skipped on Linux aarch64:
# PyPI rasterio >=1.4.4 declares `click!=8.2.*` and has no cp312 aarch64 wheel before 1.4.4), so
# this lock carries click 8.2.1 and rasterio 1.4.3 -- the x86_64 resolution.
#
# Note: CI resolves without Serverless grpcio-status constraints; the protobuf version
# in this lock (6.x) reflects the mapbox-vector-tile>=2.2 floor, NOT a CI grpcio constraint.
# The real runtime protobuf is set by the Serverless base image.

# Local package — the base dependencies plus [stac], [vizx] and [zarr_dbr19] from pyproject.toml
.[stac,vizx,zarr_dbr19]

# The env6 runtimes' preinstalled versions (DBR 19, Serverless env 6): pandas 2.3.3, numpy 2.3.4,
# urllib3 2.5.0, click 8.2.1 (the floor stops a downgrade to 8.1.8). The plain wheel has floors
# only; these holds keep the lock at the runtime family's versions.
pandas<2.4
numpy<2.4
urllib3<2.6
click>=8.2,<8.3; platform_machine != "aarch64"
mapbox-vector-tile>=2.2
rio-tiler>=9.0,<10

# pyspark is NOT a geobrix base dependency (Databricks provides it on every supported
# runtime; see pyproject.toml). This lock is for local/manual verification off-cluster,
# so pin it explicitly — same floor the base dependency used to carry.
pyspark>=4.0.0

# pillow is resolved through [vizx] (matplotlib, scikit-image, imageio, contextily) and certifi
# through requests and httpx2; the floors keep a regenerated lock at the security-patched
# releases. CI-only: the extras in pyproject.toml are unchanged, and pip leaves the runtime's own
# pillow and certifi in place.
pillow>=13.0.0
certifi>=2026.10.19
